**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1 | Deliver Requested Resources | Ensure that every requested resource is collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | **#** | **Achieve** | – | Parallelism is required because several items may be requested from different storages; each can be handled by a distinct robot, reducing overall mission time. |
| G2 | Collection Phase | Execute all actions needed to obtain the resources from storage. | **;** | **Perform** | **AND** with G3 | Sequential: collection must finish before delivery starts. |
| G3 | Delivery Phase | Execute all actions needed to transport the collected resources to the destination. | **;** | **Perform** | **AND** with G2 | Sequential: delivery only begins after collection succeeds. |
| G4 | Go to Storage | Navigate to the storage location that contains the requested resource. | **;** | **Perform** | **AND** with G9, G5 | Must be performed before any request can be sent. |
| G5 | Request Resource | Send a message to the storage specifying the exact resources needed and wait for confirmation. | **;** | **Perform** | **AND** with G6 | Request must precede waiting for retrieval. |
| G6 | Wait for Retrieval | Remain idle until the storage confirms that the requested resources have been retrieved. | **-** | **Perform** | – | Leaf goal – no further decomposition. |
| G7 | Make Runs to Destination | Perform one or more trips from the robot’s current position to the specified destination, carrying the retrieved resources. | **;** | **Perform** | **AND** with G8 | Each run is a distinct action that must be performed before checking battery status. |
| G8 | Check Battery Low 30% (Delivery) | Query the robot’s battery level; if it is below 30 % trigger a fallback. | **FALLBACK(G7, G14)** | **Query** | – | The mission must continue normally unless battery is low; thus a fallback is needed. |
| G9 | Check Battery Low 10% (Collection) | Query the robot’s battery level; if it is below 10 % trigger a fallback. | **FALLBACK(G5, G12)** | **Query** | – | Collection must be aborted early to avoid depletion; fallback handles this case. |
| G10 | Return to Recharging Station | Navigate back to the nearest recharging station. | **-** | **Perform** | – | Leaf goal – robot simply returns. |
| G11 | Assign Mission to Another Robot (Collection) | Inform another available robot to take over the remaining collection task. | **-** | **Perform** | – | After low‑battery handling, the mission must be reassigned. |
| G12 | Return Resource to Checkpoint | If battery drops to 30 % during delivery, return the resource to a predefined checkpoint. | **-** | **Perform** | – | Ensures that partially delivered resources are safely stored. |
| G13 | Assign Remaining Task (Delivery) | Inform another robot of the remaining runs needed to finish the delivery. | **-** | **Perform** | – | Allows the new robot to continue from the checkpoint. |
| G14 | Trigger Alert & Report (Failure) | If the resource cannot be returned to the checkpoint, send an alert and report to the sector manager. | **-** | **Perform** | – | Failure handling goal. |

